ch that, if agreed upon, they would certainly have been included in the document in the view of the court, then evidence of their alleged making must be kept from the trier of fact. Cross References: Point 3: Sections 1–303, 2–207, 2–302 and 2–316. Definitional Cross References: “Agreed” and “agreement”. Section 1–201. “Course of dealing”. Section 1–303. “Course of performance”. Section 1–303. “Party”. Section 1–201. “Term”. Section 1–201. “Usage of trade”. Section 1–303. “Written” and “writing”. Section 1–201. § 2–202ARTICLE 2. SALES"